course: dictionary
lesson: 1295
title: Little word, many jobs: by
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «By» is one of the most common words in English, and it has lots of jobs. The clues are in the words around it. «A book by Roald Dahl» tells you who wrote the book, because by shows who did something. «Go by bus» tells you how you travel.
explain: Look for the job «by» is doing in the sentence. «Cars and railings by the sea rust quickly» uses by to mean next to. «He must get up by 7:00» uses by to mean not later than 7:00. Ask yourself: is it telling me who, how, where, when or how much?
explain: In maths, by is a signal word. «Multiply 6 by 2» tells you to multiply, and «a room 4 by 5 metres» gives you the two sides. Ask: what word would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: «By» can show who did something: «designed by someone».
fact: «By» can show how something is done: «by bus», «by hand», «win by tricks».
fact: «By» can mean next to: «sit by the window».
fact: «By» can mean not later than: «be home by six».
fact: In maths, «by» names the number you multiply or divide by: «6 divided by 2», or the sides of a shape: «4 by 5 metres».
fact: In phrases, «by» means alone, one at a time or from memory: «by myself», «one by one», «by heart».
exercise: «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone.» What does by show here? | *Who did it | What time it happened | How far away it is | How much it weighs
exercise: «Breakfast takes 20 minutes, so he must get up by 7:00.» What does by mean here? | Exactly 7:00 and no other time | Past 7:00 | *Not later than 7:00 | Next to 7:00
exercise: In «a room 4 by 5 metres», what does by tell you? | The colour of the room | *The two sides of the room | The time it took to build | The number of people who live there
test: «Ella goes to school by bus.» What does by show? | Next to the bus | Who does it | *How it is done | Past the bus
test: In «12 divided by 3», what is 3 doing? | The name of the sum | The answer to the sum | The place where you sit | *The number you divide by
exam: «The total increased by a factor of 2 by the conclusion of the week.» What does the second by mean? | *Not later than the end of the week | Next to the week | Past the week | Because of the week
